    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on dynamic speed and favorable platoon matchups. Our top play is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), whose matchup against McGreevy provides an elite ceiling bolstered by a +14% platoon adjustment and an advantageous spot at the top of the order. **Junior Caminero** (74.75) and **Christian Yelich** (70.33) follow close behind; **Caminero** benefits significantly from a favorable 5.02 xERA matchup against Quantrill, while **Christian Yelich** leverages a strong platoon advantage against Roupp. We are also leaning heavily on **Trea Turner** (70.26), whose BvP history and leadoff status make him a core contributor despite the respectable 4.34 xERA of Alcantara.\n\nThe most challenging decision today was the exclusion of **Chase Meidroth** (36.07), who failed to clear our 40.0 floor threshold. Despite a decent base projection, his matchup against the elite Cole (3.51 xERA) and a suboptimal #8 spot in the order cratered his efficiency score. Conversely, we are carrying some risk with **Yordan Alvarez** (53.45) and **Gary Sanchez** (47.85), both of whom are confirmed pending lineup verification. While **Yordan Alvarez** remains a start despite the negative platoon edge against Detmers due to his elite xwOBA, his score reflects the volatility of that matchup. Meanwhile, **Caleb Durbin** remains an essential start at 55.02; while he faces a tougher arm in Jump, his role as a primary stolen base threat is vital for our league-wide strategy, even when park factors fluctuate.",
